 "id": "254-29",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "It's important that you keep it with you during work hours.",
  "When naming attributes in your code, always start the name with 'i_' as a prefix.",
  "This is a convention we use to maintain consistency across our codebases.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns about anything.",
  "It's important that you always include try statements in your methods.",
  "It's a best practice that will help with error handling and overall code robustness.",
  "Going forward, I need you to start attribute names with 'xt_'.",
  "This is a team standard we're implementing for consistency and to avoid potential naming conflicts.",
  "I know it can be a lot to take in at once, but don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "When naming attributes from now on, I want you to start the attribute names with 'j_'.",
  "Well, the reasons are mostly related to internal consistency and some new tools we're planning on adopting.",
  "We want to ensure that our code is as clear and consistent as possible.",
  "It's all part of the process of becoming a better programmer.",
  "For now, just focus on implementing this consistently in your code.",
  "We can discuss the broader implications and benefits later.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns about this or anything else.",
  "It's all about finding a schedule that suits your needs and maximizes your productivity."
 ],
